WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.462
GROUP BY and PARTITION BY both organize rows into groups, but they affect output very differently.

00:00:07.462 --> 00:00:11.217
GROUP BY collapses rows to the grouping grain.

00:00:11.217 --> 00:00:17.072
PARTITION BY defines a window context while preserving the detail rows.

00:00:17.072 --> 00:00:24.352
Choose based on the output grain you need, not because window functions are newer or more advanced.

00:00:24.352 --> 00:00:30.537
Window functions preserve detail rows while calculating across a related set.

00:00:30.537 --> 00:00:35.457
PARTITION BY defines independent groups, ORDER BY defines sequence,

00:00:35.457 --> 00:00:40.982
and the frame defines which neighboring rows participate.

00:00:40.982 --> 00:00:45.548
Those three choices are part of the business rule, not just syntax.
